**Async** (`async: true`). Job accepted and queued. Poll `GET /api/v1/releases/jobs/{jobId}`
until `status` is `complete` or `failed`. `result.analysisJson` holds the analysis;
`result.release` holds the release record (omitted when `analyzeOnly=true`).

post.description:
Registers a new outbound webhook endpoint. The `secret` is returned **only once** in this response — store it securely. Processors signs each delivery payload as `HMAC-SHA256(secret, "${timestamp}.${rawBody}")` and sends it in `X-MailDrip-Signature: sha256=<hex>`. Verify on your end:
```js const crypto = require("crypto"); function verifySignature(secret, timestamp, rawBody, sigHeader) {
  const expected = "sha256=" + crypto
    .createHmac("sha256", secret)
    .update(`${timestamp}.${rawBody}`)
    .digest("hex");
  return crypto.timingSafeEqual(Buffer.from(sigHeader), Buffer.from(expected));
} ```
